 pudding","dish/pease-pudding"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Racuchy","dish/racuchy"],["Rosół","dish/roso"],["Šakotis","dish/sakotis"],["Salceson","dish/salceson"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Steak tartare","dish/steak-tartare"],["Streuselkuchen","dish/streuselkuchen"],["Székelykáposzta","dish/szekelykaposzta"],["Tsvikli","dish/tsvikli"],["Uszka","dish/uszka"],["Zapiekanka","dish/zapiekanka"],["Zrazy","dish/zrazy"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/2/24/Golabki_jacek.jpg/500px-Golabki_jacek.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Jacaldinho1","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Golabki_jacek.jpg"}},"ingredient/shark-meat":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/shark-meat","n":"Shark meat","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 3 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Shark meat is a seafood consisting of the flesh of sharks. Several sharks are fished for human consumption, such as porbeagles, dogfish sharks, requiem shark, and salmon sharks, among others. Shark meat is popular in Asia, where it is often consumed dried, smoked, or salted. The largest consumer of shark meat in the world is Brazil, but it is also consumed regularly in Iceland, Japan, Australia, parts of India, parts of Canada, the United States, Sri Lanka, areas of Africa, Mexico and Yemen. China is a large consumer of shark meat and are primary contributors to loss of shark populations in the pacific."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-shark-meat"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark_meat"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Imitation shark fin soup","dish/imitation-shark-fin-soup"],["Shark fin soup","dish/shark-fin-soup"]]],["Icelandic cuisine","cuisine/icelandic-cuisine",[["Hákarl","dish/hakarl"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Greenland shark","ingredient/greenland-shark"],["Shark's fin","ingredient/shark-s-fin"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/b/b3/CazoneteDSC_1332.jpg/500px-CazoneteDSC_1332.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"CostaPPPR","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CazoneteDSC_1332.jpg"}},"dish/nesselrode-pudding":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/nesselrode-pudding","n":"Nesselrode pudding","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Russian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Nesselrode pudding is a French chestnut-based frozen dessert invented in the first half of the 19th century and named after Russian diplomat Karl Nesselrode.  The dish spawned a number of variations, including an American pie; other chestnut-flavored dishes also received Nesselrode's name, not only desserts but also savory dishes such as consommé and sweetbreads."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-nesselrode-pudding"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nesselrode_pudding"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Currant","ingredient/currant"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Maraschino","ingredient/maraschino"],["Powdered sugar","ingredient/powdered-sugar"],["Sponge cake","ingredient/sponge-cake"],["Succade","ingredient/succade"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Russian cuisine","links":[["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Blini","dis