, Hainan, Japan, Myanmar, Taiwan, Nepal, Thailand, and Vietnam. In China it grows in the provinces of Guizhou, Sichuan, Hainan, and Yunnan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-osmanthus-fragrans"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osmanthus_fragrans"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Osmanthus cake","dish/osmanthus-cake"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Goji","ingredient/goji"],["Rock candy","ingredient/rock-candy"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/e/ea/Osmanthus_fragrans_%28orange_flowers%29.jpg/500px-Osmanthus_fragrans_%28orange_flowers%29.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Laitr Keiows","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osmanthus_fragrans_(orange_flowers).jpg"}},"dish/pao-de-lo":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pao-de-lo","n":"Pão de Ló","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Portuguese cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pão de Ló is a Portuguese sponge cake made of eggs, sugar, and wheat flour. Unlike other cakes or breads, yeast or baking powder is generally not used. Rather, to provide volume, air is suspended into the cake batter during mixing."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pao-de-lo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P%C3%A3o_de_L%C3%B3"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Food From Portugal","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"foodfromportugal.com","note":"Portuguese-run recipe site and video channel of traditional Portuguese dishes.","url":"https://www.foodfromportugal.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Portuguese cuisi